+### `meta.json` scale vs physical frame
+
+`scale` is **grid cells per voxel of this mesh's own scan** (e.g. `0.05` means a
+20-voxel step).  It is correct within one file.  It does **not** identify which
+physical scan the coordinates belong to.  Segments often ship several meshes
+that all declare the same `scale` while their voxel sizes differ by up to ~40×
+(villa #1522).  Coordinates from those meshes must not be compared using `scale`
+alone.
+
+Optional field:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|-------|---------|
+| `voxel_size_um` | Isotropic µm per voxel of the scan this mesh was written in |
+
+When present, consumers can tell frames apart without parsing directory names.
+`vesuvius.tifxyz.meta_frames` can parse the conventional `-<float>um` token from
+a directory name, annotate an existing `meta.json`, and report same-`scale` /
+different-voxel-size ambiguity across a segment `mesh/` tree.
+
+
 ## Quick Start
 
 ```python
